    "summary": "The configurator won't put a drawer and a spike at the same corner of a cell. I built a nearby layout it does accept: a drawer and a spike on the same cell, at different corners, so they don't touch.\n\nCell (0,0) is now a north-half base with a drawer (drawer:0#0,0#cut) on its cut face. I tried a spike at the corner on the drawer's side, where cells (0,0), (1,0) and (1,-1) meet. It was refused with SPIKE_CLASH: \"a drawer (south half) fills this corner of the junction, where the spike would stand.\"\n\nInstead, a solid spike (spike:0#0,-1|0,0|1,-1) stands at the north corner of the same cell, where cells (0,0), (0,-1) and (1,-1) meet. I added two full bases at (0,-1) and (1,-1) because a spike needs three cells meeting. Caps close the open faces and joint bolts lock the bases together.\n\ncheck_build: no issues, mesh collision check clear. The build has 17 parts.",
